      },
      "beats": [
        {
          "say": "Acceptance alone leaves a probability deficit wherever the target wants more mass than the proposer supplies. On rejection, draw a replacement from the positive part of target minus draft, normalized by its sum. This is the residual distribution for the current prefix.",
          "start": 0.4,
          "end": 16.936,
          "duration": 16.536,
          "until": 17.536
        },
        {
          "say": "Our constructed distributions leave a deficit only on bird. The residual therefore puts all correction probability on that token. The other words can already obtain their complete target mass through accepted proposals, so they receive no additional correction mass in this example.",
          "start": 17.536,
          "end": 34.576,
          "duration": 17.04,
          "until": 35.176
        },
        {
          "say": "The total residual mass equals the overall chance of rejection. If the two distributions match exactly, that total is zero and rejection is impossible. A correct implementation avoids attempting to normalize a zero residual on a branch that cannot be reached.",
          "start": 35.176,
          "end": 52.096000000000004,
          "duration": 16.92,
          "until": 52.896
        }
      ],
